{#- Implements [WITHDRAWAL-UNLIST]: every URL the site used to serve
    (_data/retiredUrls.json) REDIRECTS to `/`, so a link from an installed
    binary, a search result, or someone's bookmark lands on the one statement
    rather than a 404 or a second copy of it.

    A meta refresh with a canonical link, not a server rule: GitHub Pages serves
    static files and has no redirect table. `noindex` plus the canonical tells a
    crawler that `/` is the page; `0;` makes a browser move immediately, and the
    body link is there for the seconds before it does and for anything that
    ignores the refresh. The refresh target is root-relative so a preview build
    or the test server redirects within itself; the canonical stays absolute
    because that is what a crawler needs.

    No copy lives here. This page says nothing the statement does not, because
    it is not a page — it is a doorway to one. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}/">
<title>{{ withdrawal.title }}</title>
</head>
<body>
<p><a href="/">{{ withdrawal.title }} — read the statement.</a></p>
</body>
</html>
